From 5c76aa9510eae440cc13d756d1bfd3942229d9ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sento Daimon <339524263+sentodaimon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:09:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Coin Series stage 5: claim snapshot and claim transactions

- claim snapshot: Bitcoin Core UTXO snapshot format (dumptxoutset), verified once against the
  consensus serialized hash (main/test: Bitcoin Core assumeutxo value for height 840,000) and the
  snapshot block hash; sparse txid index cached next to the file; node refuses to start on
  main/test without it (-allowmissingsnapshot for development)
- coins view layer shows unclaimed snapshot outputs as coins (amount x multiplier, sentinel height);
  claim marker coins in the chainstate record claims atomically and are removed on disconnect
- claim transaction (version CLM1): only snapshot outputs, all inputs final, no lock time,
  one proof per input (<= 10,000 bytes), <= 500 inputs; normal transactions cannot spend snapshot outputs
- ownership proofs: BIP-322 simple / full or legacy signed message (P2PKH) over a message committing
  to rule version, chain and environment, genesis, snapshot hash and claim txid; verified with
  Bitcoin's original signature rules; time-locked and unprefixed proofs rejected
- coinbase must carry the tag 'coin-series' after the height (new txids never equal Bitcoin's)
- policy: claim version standard, fixed sigop cost per proof
- RPCs: getsnapshotinfo, getclaimable, createclaim, getclaimmessage, addclaimproof, signclaimwithkey
- contrib/coinseries/claim_smoke.sh end-to-end test
